## 5. Methodology

### 5.1 Justification

The Scrum methodology is well-suited for the VR Learning Platform project due to its iterative and flexible nature. Scrum allows for continuous feedback and adaptation, which is crucial for a project involving cutting-edge technology like VR. The project will be divided into six sprints, each focusing on specific deliverables, such as the development of the VR environment, integration with the LMS, and user training. Daily stand-up meetings, sprint reviews, and retrospectives will ensure that the project stays on track and that any issues are addressed promptly.

Scrum also promotes collaboration and transparency, which are essential for a project with multiple stakeholders, including students, lecturers, and IT staff. By using Scrum, the project team can ensure that the final product meets the needs of all stakeholders and delivers maximum value.

